''' Furis Incarnon Genesis''' is an item that is used to add [[Incarnon]] upgrades to the {{Weapon|Furis}} or {{Weapon|1=Mk1-Furis}}.

==Acquisition==
*Upon completion of [[The Duviri Paradox]] and [[Angels of the Zariman]], and unlocking [[The Steel Path]], players can earn {{Resource|1=Furis Incarnon Genesis}} from [[The Circuit]]'s Steel Path to place on their Furis with the help of [[Cavalero]] in the [[Chrysalith]]. This [[Incarnon Genesis]] form grants it evolutions to a transformation and newfound strength.
*Purchased from Cavalero for {{pc|120}}, complete with the resources used in its installation. This purchase can only be made '''once'''.

==Incarnon Genesis==

===Evolutions===
*Installing the Furis Incarnon Genesis requires 20 {{Resource|Pathos Clamp|Pathos Clamps}}, 70 {{Resource|Yao Shrub|Yao Shrubs}}, and 80 {{Resource|Lamentus}}.
*When installed, the first Evolution tier is unlocked. The following Evolution tiers, their requirements for unlocking them, and their related perks, are shown below; 
**Each challenge additionally grants 5,000 [[affinity]] to the weapon, affected by [[Affinity Booster]]s.

====Evolution I====
*Weakpoint hits charge Incarnon Transmutation; Alt Fire transmutes. Switching back will expend any remaining charge.
*Project a wide {{D|Heat}} Damage beam.
**Incarnon Form fires a short-ranged, wide {{Weapon|Klamora Prism}}-like beam that deals pure {{D|Heat}} damage and has significantly increased base damage, [[Critical Chance]], [[Critical Multiplier]], [[Status Chance]], and [[Fire Rate]], but has linear [[Damage Falloff]] from 100% to 80% from 10m to 16m target distance and has a maximum range of '''16''' meters.
**Due to not being able to be equipped with {{M|Ruinous Extension}}, its damage falloff is affected by [[Projectile Speed]], but the beam length isn't. Thus, it is possible to completely negate falloff with sufficient Projectile Speed.
**The beam has no innate punch-through effect.
*Mode switching is '''not''' instantaneous and has an animation equal to the weapon's [[reload speed]].
*Incarnon Form is activated by filling the Incarnon Transmutation gauge that appears under the reticule by achieving [[Enemy Body Parts|weakpoint hits]] and then pressing the [[Alternate Fire]] button. '''20''' weakpoints will completely fill the gauge. A full gauge is not required to activate Incarnon Form.
**Charges do '''not''' generate on the backpacks of most [[MOA]] variants, or vulnerability spots generated by {{A|Sonar}} or {{M|Detect Vulnerability}} in places other than actual weakpoints.
**Weakpoints on corpses or [[Invulnerable]] targets do '''not''' build charges.
**Individual [[Multishot]] bullets can build charges.
*Instead of drawing ammunition from its reserves, the Furis's Incarnon Form uses a separate "magazine" with each charge producing '''14''' rounds to a maximum of '''280'''. Once all ammunition is expended, the Furis reverts to its normal form.
**Incarnon Form's magazine is '''not''' affected by mods.
**Incarnon Form is '''not''' affected by [[Ammo Efficiency]] (such as {{A|Energized Munitions}}).
**Charges and Incarnon Form persists through all activities, such as holstering, [[bleedout]], or being [[disarm]]ed. However, charges and Incarnon Form are removed upon [[death]].
*Swapping to and from Incarnon Form will fully reload the normal form's magazine.

====Evolution II====
*''Unlock Challenge:'' Complete a solo mission with this weapon equipped.
*Perk 1: '''Haven Foray:'''
**Increase Damage by '''+28''' (Furis) / '''+34''' (Mk1).
**With Overshields: Increase Damage by '''+30'''.
*Perk 2: '''Stormburst:'''
**Increase Damage by '''+28''' (Furis) / '''+34''' (Mk1).
**On hitting enemies affected by {{D|Electricity}} Status: '''+0.4''' Multishot for '''2s'''. Stacks up to '''3x'''.

====Evolution III====
*''Unlock Challenge:'' Kill '''100''' enemies with this weapon's Incarnon Form.
*Perk 1: '''Practiced Grip:'''
**Increase Accuracy by '''+50%'''
*Perk 2: '''Extended Volley:'''
**Increase Magazine Capacity by '''+25'''.
*Perk 3: '''Executioner's Fortune:'''
**On Headshot: '''10%''' chance for Instant Reload

====Evolution IV====
*''Unlock Challenge:'' Kill '''30''' enemies afflicted with '''4''' or more status effects.
**{{Arcane|Secondary Encumber}}, {{WF|Voruna}}'s {{A|Fangs of Raksh}}, and {{WF|Citrine}}'s {{A|Fractured Blast}} and {{A|Prismatic Gem}} are effective at spreading numerous status effects. Consider reducing [[Ability Strength]] so these abilities do not take away Furis's kills.
*Perk 1: '''Headcracker:'''
**On Headshot: +'''5%''' Fire Rate for '''2s'''. Stacks up to '''10x'''.
*Perk 2: '''Prelude of Might:'''
**With Critical Chance below '''40%''': Increase Base Critical Damage Multiplier by '''+3x'''.
***Note: Base increase only applies to incarnon mode and is not correctly reflected in the arsenal. In normal mode this is a flat +3x increase and accurately reflected in the arsenal.
*Perk 3: '''Elemental Balance:'''
**Increase Status Chance by '''+28%''' (Furis) / '''+39%''' (Mk1).

